In article <lumpi.730869820@dobag> lumpi@dobag.in-berlin.de (Joern Lubkoll) writes:
>hi,
>
>i'm playing a level 18 babarian and i'm trying to write some nice scrolls
>of genocide. But when a)pplying my magic marker and entering the letter of
>the blank scroll to write on and the name of the scroll to write, nethack
>will always respond with 'your marker is to dry to write with'.
>
>why ? What can i do against that ?

Magic markers get a limited # charges. (ID the marker to see how many
charges it has.) Every time you write a scroll or spellbook, you use
up some charges; the bigger the spell, the more charges you use up.
When you run out of charges, you get the "too dry to write" message.

You can recharge a magic marker with a scroll of charging.
